Guess I'll see you there!

137
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:30,960
Before long, his journey led him
to the lawless area of our country.

138
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:38,637
It was a place where criminals and exiled
Ronan from various regions ran rampant.

139
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:43,480
As one can imagine, it was full
of theft, violence, and bloodshed.

140
00:09:43,660 --> 00:09:48,280
This hell was so far beyond saving that
even the Shogun's family turned away.

141
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:50,000
Its name was Kuri.

142
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,900
I could get used to this.

143
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:59,251
It was like fate itself brought him there.

144
00:09:59,400 --> 00:10:02,459
That day, Lord Odin strode
into his soon-to-be home.

145
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:05,237
Soon after, Kuri's most
wicked man appeared.

146
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:08,438
He had his band of thugs
and was looking for trouble.

147
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:17,440
Ashura Doji was his name.

148
00:10:17,700 --> 00:10:19,171
They clashed immediately.

149
00:11:01,460 --> 00:11:05,380
With one artful strike, Lord
Odin brought down his foe.

150
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:11,400
Remarkably, with his victory, also
came the loyalty of Doji's underlings.

151
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:18,520
Wow, he was something.

152
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,073
Swooped in like a hero.

153
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,068
He was a remarkable fellow.

154
00:11:22,380 --> 00:11:25,086
His actions even helped
Kuri in its formation.

155
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:28,800
Major changes followed.

156
00:11:29,140 --> 00:11:31,669
He taught and gave the
ruffians work to do.

157
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:39,420
Buildings began to pop up And
the castle too Then ultimately,

158
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:42,485
the Paradise Farm was
launched for the citizens

159
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:49,417
This once wasteland
Transformed into a vibrant

160
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:53,040
region full of laughter
and prosperity At last,

161
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:58,160
Lord Odin was bestowed the well-earned
title of Daimyo By the Shogun Sukiyaki

162
00:12:00,620 --> 00:12:05,180
incredible to think how much this man
accomplished by the mere age of 20

163
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:13,497
he dug out a river built docks connected

164
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:16,740
with neighboring regions
and other people too

165
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:21,800
you know what i mean

166
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:26,260
i must admit i agree completely

167
